        // ------------------------------------------------------------------
        // Heading-hold rings — one 4 km ring per airframe, centers along z = -58000.
        // Planes spawn evenly around the ring flying tangentially (heading =
        // bearing + 90°), so each ring expands outward instead of converging.
        // Every heading-hold plane has its own altitude, 50 m apart: generic
        // 2600–3350, business 3400–3950, tanker 4000–4350, cargo 4400–4750, and
        // electric low at 1400–1950 (its validated envelope tops out near 2000 m).
        // Heavies fly a half tank to keep stall margin in the thinner air.
